function <m>\rho(x, y, z) = 1</m>.</p>
<p>A. Determine the mass of the wire: <fillin characters="30" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
<p>B. Determine the coordinates of the center of mass: (<fillin characters="10" name="AnSwEr0002"/>, <fillin characters="10" name="AnSwEr0003"/>, <fillin characters="10" name="AnSwEr0004"/>)</p>
<p>C. Determine the moment of inertia about the z-axis: <fillin characters="30" name="AnSwEr0005"/></p>
<p><alert> Note: </alert> If a wire with linear density <m>\rho(x, y, z)</m>
lies along a space curve <m>C</m>, its <alert> moment of inertia </alert>
about the z-axis is defined by <m>I_z = \int_C (x^2+y^2) \rho(x, y, z) ds</m>.</p>
</statement>
